  "volume_scope": "Supplied smooth projective meromorphic CY family with connected complex and geometrically integral generic fibres, global meromorphic relative canonical trivialization and regular projective SNC model. Published volume asymptotics and local cutoff convergence give the normalized probability weights, raw and probability comparisons and almost-full mass of fixed interior chamber charts. The dyadic application requires 1<=m<=n and reduced SNC.",
  "trace_descent_scope": "Projective geometrically integral X over C((t)), ample L, cyclic extension C((tau)) with t=tau^q and extended absolute value. Average a finite FS family by tensor products; trace-dual coefficient reconstruction gives exact equality of weighted maxima. Uniform FS approximation and analytic Galois quotient are explicit imports; continuous psh metrics descend. Arbitrary model-function descent and wild/mixed-characteristic or unbounded extensions are not claimed.",
  "ramified_hybrid_scope": "A supplied regular reduced SNC projective model of the finite cover and all prior analytic/FS/hybrid inputs. Whole child metric and potential are renormalized by 1/q, model tests give a continuous compact Hausdorff hybrid quotient, invariant continuous limit and trace descent give the parent continuous psh limit. Published q^m unnormalized skeletal pushforward cancels for probabilities.",
  "remaining_application_gates": [
    "Projective/regular reduced semistable model and meromorphic bundle/canonical presentations",
